   139  /* A bucket is a small hash table.  This one consists of a number of
   140     bucket elements plus some bookkeeping fields.  The number of elements
   141     depends on the optimum blocksize for the storage device and on a
   142     parameter given at file creation time.  This bucket takes one block.
   143     When one of these tables gets full, it is split into two hash buckets.
   144     The contents are split between them by the use of the first few bits
   145     of the 31 bit hash function.  The location in a bucket is the hash
   146     value modulo the size of the bucket.  The in-memory images of the
   147     buckets are allocated by malloc using a calculated size depending of
   148     the file system buffer size.  To speed up write, each bucket will have
   149     BUCKET_AVAIL avail elements with the bucket. */
